WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:15.309 --> 00:00:17.259 align:start position:0%
 
again  Ghost Recon wildlands is a squad based  Tom Clancy game that plays by the  numbers it stays true to the series  Rainbow six inspired routes emulating  the cold and calculated nature of  organized infiltration and coordinated  stealth kills unfortunately the  adherence to the specific kind of  gameplay gets lost and diluted in wild  lands as vast expanse of Bolivia a  revenge tale disguised as a narco-state  destabilization operation is low-hanging  fruit worse yet the narrative  perpetuates the notion that a cartel is  only worth taking seriously when one of  your own has been tortured today  ignoring the thousands of locals who  suffered similar fates it's easy to tell  that Karen Bowman your CIA field handler  has a personal vendetta against the  Santa Blanca a drug cartel that rules  Bolivia when you ultimately come  face-to-face with El sueño their cartels  kingpin you can spot the payoff a mile  away at the end there's no poignant  message or lesson regarding this latest  Tom Clancy episode in American  interventionism target on my back  waiting for someone else could come to  the crown the pursuit of a single lead  that Karen provides conveniently results  in a series of other clues and each one  of those tip-offs blossoms into others  enough successful missions eventually  results in confrontations with under  bosses and lieutenants who are less than  six degrees away from El sueño some of  your Intel will reveal locations of  weapons to add to your collection  so amassing a stockpile of firearms is  purely optional compared to the  multitude of games where the acquisition  of guns is a major selling point  wild lines of selection is serviceable  the problem is that you can easily  complete the game with your initial  loadout where the fans who've been  hooked on Ghost Recon for the advancing  technologies the lack of gadgetry and  wildlands will prove this appointing the  novel appeal of drones has long since  expired well you can upgrade it with a  handful of offensive and diversionary  capabilities its default function as a  target marking device is all you need  while the drone marks your targets it's  your squads responsibility to pull off  the kills the need for coordination  underscores the team-based appeal of  wildlife which can be experienced with a  I control teammates or preferably with  other players when playing with skilled  friends  comfort in knowing that you'll most  likely be on the same page  playing with AI has its own benefits  like being better bullet sponges when  they're out in the open Healing you one  puzzling omission to multi player is the  ability to form a mixed squad of friends  in AI if you're only playing with one  buddy you're stuck as a pair wildlands  is most gratifying moments come from  playing the ghost it means having the  patience to spend minutes surveying a  stronghold from a distance and arming  yourself with that visual information to  confidently infiltrate the base equally  thrilling other moments where you have  little time to adapt to changing  circumstances when the best laid plans  go wrong when you've been spotted and a  base is on high alert you're treated to  one of the few instances where your  squad mates moment to moment updates are  actually useful when a high-value target  is fleeing your team will let you know  at the outset it appears that wild lines  of strength is in its diverse mission  types for every assassination there's a  capture or rescue assignment you might  even find yourself pulling off the old  switcharoo with two similar looking  trucks group I got no idea who that is  don't [ __ ] me Hernando you had to  tell me where I can find Reed or I make  sure El sueño knows all about your  little human trafficking rings it's  never a dull moment at least for the  first 20 or so hours by the time you've  experienced these kinds of objectives a  handful of times boredom sets in the mix  of dense vegetation and barren mountains  of Bolivia echo the environments of  Metal Gear Solid 5 the phantom pain just  less accommodating navigating your way  down a rocky cliff on foot is as  unpredictable as climbing one instead  you're left using vehicles as your most  reliable means of traversal yet for a  map that should be more off-road  friendly this interpretation of Bolivia  often Courage's you to keep to the  beaten path  lest you wipeout after a sick cliff jump  on a motorcycle as only the second  open-world game in the clan severs Ghost  Recon wildlands is a middling Lee safe  tactical shooter with a slightly wasted  opportunity given the ambitious scope of  its seemingly boundless map while its  main strength is its mission diversity  it doesn't take long to lose the  motivation after reaching El sueño  doorstep even with a foursome of  highly-trained friends wild lads  eventually reveals its demented  in return the feeling of positive  immediacy and dopamine hits begins to  wane sooner than you expected from a  game with such a large and diverse world  [Music]

